                <pb facs="0340" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4217: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-17T13:00:00-05:00">April 17, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Department’s telegram no. 84, April 16, 7 p.m. With a view to avoiding any
                    undue anticipation or even misunderstanding as to the scope of the contemplated
                    modifications and since they will not improbably form a part of a general scheme
                    of financial relations between the two countries, I respectfully suggest that
                    the (to Lescot presumably) good news be reserved for communication to him at the
                    Department during the exchange of views envisaged in the Department’s telegram
                    83, April 16, midnight [<hi rendition="#italic">5 p.m.</hi>]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
